<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Governs Auto Backup on API 31+ (cloud-backup) and the device-to-device "Copy your data"
     transfer (device-transfer). Excludes only what would be actively wrong to restore, not
     everything: with no <include> elements, everything else (e.g. HolderSettings' small UI
     preferences: theme, font, sync interval) is backed up by default. See backup_rules.xml for
     the equivalent pre-API-31 rules.

     Excluded:
     - files/holder/, holder-core's SQLite index and any local working files. This is a
       rebuildable cache, not a copy of record (Git is); restoring a stale one on a different
       install could also resurrect plaintext local state for an encrypted_git project onto a
       device that never had it.
     - files/local_state/, small Android-side markers that must never survive a restore onto a
       different install, e.g. SnapshotProtection's guard against SnapshotWorker overwriting
       an unread inbound snapshot (see git/backup/SnapshotProtection.kt), which only works
       *because* it can't be carried over the way HolderSettings' DataStore prefs (below) are.
     - shared_prefs/holder_platform_keyring.xml, AndroidKeyringStore's secrets (Git signing
       keys, S3 credentials), AES-GCM encrypted with a non-exportable AndroidKeyStore key. That
       key never leaves this device's secure hardware, so a restored copy of this file would be
       ciphertext nothing can ever decrypt again, worse than losing it outright, since it would
       look "connected" in Settings while silently unable to do anything, rather than plainly
       needing to be reconnected.
     - files/datastore/github_credential.preferences_pb, the dedicated encrypted GitHub
       credential state, protected by the same non-exportable device key for the same reason.
     - files/editor-recovery-drafts/, the editor's copies of text not yet saved into a card
       (editor/EditorRecoveryStore.kt). Device-local by design: they name projects and cards
       that only exist on this install (files/holder/ isn't restored), so on another device
       they could never be saved and would sit there as plaintext card text indefinitely.

     Cloud backup requires client-side encryption (issue #355): disableIfNoEncryptionCapabilities
     stops the whole cloud backup, not just the snapshot, on a device that can't encrypt it with
     a client-side secret (backup on, but no screen lock). The snapshot below is readable card
     text (gzip, not encryption), deliberately not tied to the old device's Keystore so a
     new phone can restore it, so the backup transport has to supply the confidentiality.
     That's separate from a project's encrypted_git mode, which protects the Git remote, not
     this copy. Device-to-device transfer never goes through a server and stays unconditional.

     Included (no rule needed, it's just not inside an exclusion above):
     - files/backup/snapshot.jsonl.gz, SnapshotWriter's gzip-compressed rolling export of recent
       cards. This is the one piece of card content deliberately NOT excluded; unlike
       files/holder/, it's a purpose-built, self-contained export rather than a live index, so
       it doesn't carry either of the two risks above. See git/backup/SnapshotWriter.kt.
     - files/datastore/, HolderSettings' own DataStore preferences (theme, font, sync interval,
       and the one-time offer flags), deliberately small, low-stakes UI state, fine to carry
       over. See git/backup/SnapshotProtection.kt's doc comment for the one place this default
       inclusion needed a *separate*, non-backed-up guard rather than just living with it. -->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup disableIfNoEncryptionCapabilities="true">
        <exclude domain="file" path="holder/" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="local_state/" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="holder_platform_keyring.xml" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="datastore/github_credential.preferences_pb" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="editor-recovery-drafts/" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="file" path="holder/" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="local_state/" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="holder_platform_keyring.xml" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="datastore/github_credential.preferences_pb" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="editor-recovery-drafts/" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
